1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,030
America and Britain almost went to war.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,790
Over one pig.

3
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:07,180
A farmer caught it eating his potatoes.

4
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:08,610
So he shot it.

5
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:08,950
Problem:

6
00:00:08,970 --> 00:00:10,736
the farmer was American.

7
00:00:10,756 --> 00:00:12,530
The pig was British.

8
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:14,079
He offered ten dollars.

9
00:00:14,099 --> 00:00:15,940
The owner wanted a hundred.

10
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:18,726
Worse, both countries claimed the island.

11
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:21,530
America sent over four hundred soldiers.

12
00:00:21,810 --> 00:00:23,889
Britain sent five warships.

13
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,210
The governor wanted the Americans gone.

14
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,910
The admiral said no.

15
00:00:27,930 --> 00:00:29,220
Not over a pig.

16
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:31,672
So both sides just stayed.

17
00:00:31,692 --> 00:00:33,277
For twelve years.

18
00:00:33,470 --> 00:00:34,640
And partied together.

19
00:00:34,760 --> 00:00:36,964
Then a German emperor settled it.

20
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,810
The island went to America.

21
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:40,090
Total casualties:

22
00:00:40,190 --> 00:00:41,110
one pig.

23
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:43,140
Team farmer, or team pig?
